# Healthcare Use Case: IoMT (Internet of Medical Things)
# Purpose: Ingest high-velocity streams from wearable devices (Heart Rate, O2 Saturation).
# Detect anomalies in real-time.

# ==========================================
# 1. Ingest Stream (XADD)
# ==========================================
# Device 'dev-001' sends 1 packet per second
# Stream Key: vitals:pat-123
XADD vitals:pat-123 MAXLEN ~ 10000 * hr 85 o2 98 battery 45 ts 1678886400

# ==========================================
# 2. Latest State Cache (SET)
# ==========================================
# For the dashboard "Current Status" view (no history needed)
HSET latest:pat-123 hr 85 o2 98 status "NORMAL" last_seen 1678886400

# ==========================================
# 3. TimeSeries for Trending (RedisTimeSeries)
# ==========================================
# Store efficiently for graphs (24h history)
# TS.ADD key timestamp value [LABELS label value ...]
TS.ADD ts:hr:pat-123 * 85 LABELS patient pat-123 type hr
TS.ADD ts:o2:pat-123 * 98 LABELS patient pat-123 type o2

# ==========================================
# 4. Alerting Logic (Sliding Window)
# ==========================================
# If HR > 120 for 3 consecutive readings, trigger alert.
# We can use a List to keep last N readings.

LPUSH buffer:hr:pat-123 125
LTRIM buffer:hr:pat-123 0 4 # Keep last 5

# Check logical condition (pseudocode implemented in Application or Lua)
# IF all(lrange buffer:hr:pat-123 0 2) > 120 THEN PUBLISH alert

# Alert Channel
PUBLISH alerts:nurses_station "{\"patient\": \"pat-123\", \"msg\": \"High Heart Rate\", \"val\": 125}"
